==History==
===Ben 10===
In the future, [[Kevin Levin (Original Future)|Kevin]] had been trapped in the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]] for many years. While he was there, Kevin had absorbing the powers of thousands of other aliens. During one of his breakouts, Kevin had a relationship with a woman from a [[Saturn]] colony and fathered a son named [[Devlin Levin|Devlin]].{{Refn|[[:File:Ken 10 Pop-up (18).png]]|group = pop-up|name = pop-up}}<ref name="Ken 10" /> He tricked his own son into believing that he was reformed and that he wanted to "spend some quality time with his son", and that all he had to do was to find and open the [[Null Void Projector]].

After Devlin tricked [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken Tennyson]] into showing him where the Null Void Projector was, Devlin opened the projector, releasing Kevin. When [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] found out, Kevin showed his true form. Kevin proved to be more than a match for both Ben, and Ken. When Devlin found out that he was tricked by his own father into freeing him, Devlin decided to team up with the Tennysons and fight his father.

When Ben witnessed Kevin beating up Ken and knocking him unconscious, he transformed into [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]] and beat up Kevin. When Ben and Ken walked away, Kevin got back up, proclaiming that, that was nothing. Eventually, Ken managed to toss a Null Void egg right underneath Kevin, trapping Kevin inside the bomb, and sending him back to the Null Void.

==Powers and Abilities ==
<gallery type="slideshow">
K10 (399).png|Bio-Electricity Generation
K10 (405).png|Shapeshifting
K10 (432).png|Sonic Howl
K10 (426).png|Levitation/Enhanced Digging
K10 (464).png|Enhanced Strength
K10 (394).png|Enhanced Durability
K10 (350.1).png|Enhanced Speed
K10 (456).png|Prehensile Tentacles
</gallery>
Kevin 11,000 could transform between his human and mutant forms at will. His human form does not prevent him from exhibiting powers, as human Kevin could move at a [[Kineceleran (Classic)|Kineceleran]] speeds, had enough strength to completely shatter [[Ken's Pet]] by stomping it, and could absorb electricity from [[Max Tennyson (Original Future)|Max]]'s robotic arm.

Being part-[[Galvanic Mechamorph (Classic)|Galvanic Mechamorph]], Kevin 11,000 was able to generate electricity.

Being part-[[Loboan (Classic)|Loboan]], Kevin 11,000 was able to scream sonic howls powerful enough to crack [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead's]] skin.{{Refn|[[:File:Ken 10 Pop-up (22).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Ken 10" />

Kevin 11,000 could fly or simply levitate, as he did not always need to flap his [[Lepidopterran (Classic)|Lepidopterran]] wings to fly.

Kevin 11,000 had an incredible amount of physical strength, which came from a multitude of species, one of them being [[Tetramand (Classic)|Tetramand]]. He displayed this strength when he easily knocked back Devlin in his mutant form (who likely had an identical strength level to [[Kevin 11]]), shattered crates that were bigger than him, temporarily defeating [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]], and the aforementioned stomp in human form.

Kevin 11,000 also possessed an incredible amount of enhanced durability, which also came from a multitude of species. Kevin survived all of the combined attacks of [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]], his son, and Ben 10,000, up until the latter's extreme pummeling as [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]].

Being part-[[Null Guardian]], Kevin 11,000 had prehensile tentacles.

==Weaknesses==
[[File:K10 (450).png|thumb|Electricity Vulnerability]]
Kevin 11,000 is vulnerable to electricity, as shown when he was shocked by the combination of [[Spitter|Spitter's]] liquid and [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock's]] electricity. 

